learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:28:48.217Z","harness:claude-code","A population-level survival split is the cheapest way to separate a deletion defect from an authoring gap, and it needs no code reading. Two spellings of one relation existed in this corpus - blocked_by, which the close path clears, and blocks, which it does not - and their distribution across 1,900 closed items was 1 versus 189. If under-authoring were the cause, both spellings would be scarce. The asymmetry between two encodings of the same fact is the signal; the absolute count of either one is not."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  src/cli/commands/close.ts,project,clearClosedBlockerSignals at lines 600-644; the unconditional blocked_by filter is line 626
  src/core/item/actionability.ts,project,collectBlockedByIds is the readiness consumer whose single source of truth the close path empties
  src/sdk/graph/assembly.ts,project,"blocked_by is one of three dependency reference sources feeding the graph,so the deletion removes the edge from every analytic at once"
